From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:34:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GE: split the threaded renderer into a list walker and a GL
 thread (GE_SPLIT)

With GE_SPLIT=1 the GE worker walks display lists and decodes vertices on its own core and hands every renderer call, in order, to a GL thread that owns the context (SplitRenderer). A GE job counts as completed only once the GL thread has run what it queued, interrupts are raised from the GL thread at their place in the stream, and a block transfer waits for the GL thread before guest memory moves.
Verified on desktop with the GE replay (same score and flips as the single GE thread) and screenshot comparison; on the PS Vita it ran a two-minute bot game in Vita3K. Not yet measured on a console. Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

